│ higher-quality studies and in people aged ≤ 66 years. Comorbid depression increased the risk of mortality (RR, 1.83; │
│ 95% CI, 1.00-3.36), particularly in men. Anxiety (or psychologic distress) increased the risk of COPD                │
│ outcomes/mortality in most studies (RR, 1.27; 95% CI, 1.02-1.58). Finally, COPD consistently increased the risk of   │
│ depression (RR, 1.69; 95% CI, 1.45-1.96). CONCLUSIONS Depression and anxiety adversely affect prognosis in COPD,     │
│ conferring an increased risk of exacerbation and possibly death. Conversely, COPD increases the risk of developing   │
│ depression. These bidirectional associations suggest potential usefulness of screening for these disease             │
