Review: Psychological therapies for the treatment of anxiety disorders in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease
Total studies to screen: 20

SELECTION CRITERIA:
We considered all randomised controlled trials (RCTs), cluster‐randomised trials and cross‐over trials of psychological 
therapies for people (aged over 40 years) with COPD and coexisting anxiety disorders (as confirmed by recognised 
diagnostic criteria or a validated measurement scale), where this was compared with either no intervention or education 
only. We included studies in which the psychological therapy was delivered in combination with another intervention 
(co‐intervention) only if there was a comparison group that received the co‐intervention alone.

